WEBVTT

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.340
BRENT: You are looking live
at beautiful

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.740
Porto Corsa, Italy,
on the Italian Riviera.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:16.860
What a magnificent setting for the
second race of the World Grand Prix!

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.820
DAVID: Brent, they call this place
the "Gem of the Riviera,"

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.540
and it's easy to see why.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.340
With its secluded beaches
and opulent casinos,

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.300
Porto Corsa truly is a playground
for the wealthy.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.660
And everyone who's anyone
is here today,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.500
from the ultra-rich and super-famous

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.980
to world leaders
and important dignitaries.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.820
BRENT: You aren't kidding, David.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.180
You can't do a three-point turn
without bumping into some celebrity.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.740
Welcome, everyone, to the second race
of the World Grand Prix,

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.300
where the big news
continues to be allinol.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.180
Sir Miles Axlerod spoke to the press
earlier today

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.540
to answer questions about its safety.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.380
An independent panel of scientists
has determined

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.460
that allinol is completely safe, okay?

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.060
Safe. There it is.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.820
So the race will go on, folks.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.660
But the question everyone is asking:

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.420
will the real
Lightning McQueen show up today?

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.540
BRENT: He'd better.
Talk about a home track advantage.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.540
Francesco Bernoulli
grew up racing on this course.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:15.580
ANNOUNCER: Signore e signori, in the
pole position, Numero Uno, Francesco!

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.780
Bellissima!
Thank you for your support!

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:21.420
And your big mistake, McQueen!

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.500
ANNOUNCER: In secondo position,

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:28.900
numero 95, Lightning-a McQueen-a!

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.700
McQueen-a, is-a everything OK?

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:34.580
If you're worried about your fuel, man,
don't. It's perfectly safe.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.220
No, guys,
I just really wish Mater were here.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.260
Francesco understands, McQueen.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.260
Oh, great, here it comes.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.300
What do you got, Francesco?

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:47.700
For famous race cars like Francesco
and, well, you,

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.780
to be far away from home is not easy.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:54.020
I think you forgot
the insulting part of that insult.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.660
Is-a no insult.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.700
When-a Francesco is away from home,
he misses his mama,

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.620
just like-a you miss
your tow truck amico.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.740
Gee, I maybe misjudged you,
because that's exactly...

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.020
Of course, I am at home,
and my mama is right here.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.980
Mama!

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.100
Don't worry, Mama,
McQueen is very sad.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.660
I will beat his cry-baby bottom today!

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.780
And there's the insult we were missing.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.780
(CHANTING FOR FRANCESCO)

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.420
BRENT: Darrell, the racers
are settling in as they head

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.820
to the Italian countryside.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.860
DARRELL: Whoo, boy!

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.500
This is gonna be a great race.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.180
(HORNS TOOT)

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.700
Gremlins.
Man, those are some ugly cars.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.860
Look like someone stole their trunks.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.100
(LAUGHTER)

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.660
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:11.100
My grand-a father has-a broken down.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:15.020
If-a one of-a you would help,
I would be so thankful.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.140
Sounds like you need
some roadside assistance.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.460
-She was talking to me.
-Really? Prove it.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.540
Don't-a fight over me.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.500
Signore Tow Truck, per favore.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.500
Get ready, Mater.
You're on any moment now.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.700
I don't know about this.
What if I screw things up?

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.380
FINN: Impossible.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.500
Just apply the same level of dedication

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.020
you've been using to play
the idiot tow truck, and you'll be fine.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.420
It's just that them guys look purty tough
and... Wait, did you say "idiot"?

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.540
-Is that how you see me?
-FINN: That's how everyone sees you.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.100
Isn't that the idea?

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.140
I tell you, that's the genius of it.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.220
No one realizes they're being fooled

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.980
because they're too busy laughing
at the fool.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.540
Brilliant!

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.780
-Why aren't you in disguise?
-I er...

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.740
-Come on! There's no time! Go!
-OK. OK.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.860
-Computer, disguise!
-COMPUTER: Request acknowledged.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.900
-(HORN TOOTS)
-It's the boss. He's coming.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:23.860
Ivan.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.460
Oh, er...

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:31.060
Ivan, why do you insult me so
by making me wait here?

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:40.860
He's in.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.060
BRENT: The racers are now
making their way around the hairpin

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.860
and headed downhill
toward the casino bridge.

